        "original_id": "0b6632e9-688c-5c71-94d0-f437979ca38c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Simons, Louis Gourd, Mrs. Louis Gourd\n- Organizations: College of Charleston\n- Places: Louis Gourd House, School of the Arts\n- Roles: professor, architect\n\nFacts:\n- The College of Charleston was founded in 1770 and chartered in 1785.\n- The College of Charleston is the oldest college in South Carolina, the 13th oldest institution of higher learning in the United States, and the oldest municipal college in the country.\n- In 1939, Mr. and Mrs. Louis Gourd acquired the Louis Gourd House and quickly hired Charleston architect Albert Simons to plan the building's remodeling.\n- Albert Simons was a professor at the College of Charleston for over 20 years.\n- Albert Simons started the School of the Arts at the College of Charleston.\n- The School of the Arts building is named after Albert Simons.\n- Albert Simons is honored yearly through the Simons Medal of Excellence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
